From ab6709f834ef93abeed211c75eb7594fa3216f30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Buckley <10402042+ryancbuckley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:37:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Compile wasm targets through clif-to-wasm

Wasm32/wasm64 targets get relocatable wasm objects from
clif_to_wasm::object_module::WasmObjectModule instead of cranelift-object
(no DWARF or unwind tables). The entry shim takes no arguments when the
target's main does not need argc/argv, and cfg(target_feature) reports the
wasm features.
